<!--
  ============================================================================
  ImperialVocabulary.xml                 Jawa_Patches · IMPERIAL_VOCABULARY_KEYED_1
                                         written 2026-08-21
  ============================================================================

  The Galactic Empire's vessel is Royalty's `Empire`, and Royalty's VOCABULARY
  came with it. `royalFavorLabel` was literally "honor"; 178 of Royalty's 319
  English Keyed strings say royal, title, bestowing, throne, permit or stellarch.
  This file is the second half of the fix === the first half is two ops in
  `Patches/GalacticEmpire.xml` that re-point `royalFavorLabel` to
  "Imperial favor" and `royalFavorIconPath` off Royalty's crown.

  🔑 WHY A GLOBAL KEY OVERRIDE IS SAFE HERE, and it would not be in another
  campaign. `Empire` is the ONLY def in the entire 578-mod load set carrying
  `royalFavorLabel` or `royalTitleTags` === counted against
  DefDump/defs/FactionDef.json, not assumed. Every `{FACTION_name}` these
  strings splice therefore resolves to the Galactic Empire and nobody else's
  faction can be mistranslated by them. If a mod is ever added that gives a
  SECOND faction royal titles, re-check this file before shipping.

  🔴 THIS IS A BOUNDED LIST, AND THE BOUND IS THE POINT.
  `EMPIRE_GAP_AUDIT.md` section 3: the Empire is the player's PERMANENT ENEMY, so
  all 11 `RoyalTitleDef`s, all 13 `RoyalTitlePermitDef`s and the ~25 bestowing,
  decree, hospitality and RoyalAscent quests are DARK. The player cannot earn
  favour, cannot hold a rank, cannot spend a permit, and never meets a bestower.
  ⛔ So the ~160 strings covering thrones, throne rooms, bestowing ceremonies,
  heirs, permits, "call royal aid" and the tribute collector are DELIBERATELY
  NOT TRANSLATED === no screen reaches them, and translating them would be 160
  strings of maintenance liability that nobody will ever read.

  ✅ WHAT IS LEFT IS THE SHORT LIST BELOW, and every entry is reachable for a
  reason that is written next to it. Three surfaces survive the darkening:

     1. A captured or downed Imperial who CARRIES a rank of their own.
        `Empire_Royal_*` pawn kinds still spawn and still raid us (section 3),
        and the Royalty ITab and the prisoner recruitment breakdown both read
        their rank straight off the pawn.
     2. The STAT CARD and inspect line of Imperial gear the player LOOTS.
        Prestige and cataphract armour, persona weapons and the Royalty
        implants are craftable or lootable and are explicitly NOT faction-gated
        (section 3), so their stat cards render for a colony that will never
        hold a rank.
     3. The LAW-VIOLATION letter, which is the one place the darkening makes
        MORE text reachable rather than less: a colony that loots a psychic
        amplifier and uses it gets caught by Imperial law precisely because it
        holds no rank.

  ⚠️ WHAT THIS FILE CANNOT REACH, recorded so it is not re-discovered as a bug.
  `{TITLE}` splices a `RoyalTitleDef`'s own label === freeholder, yeoman,
  knight, praetor, baron, count, consul, archon, stellarch. Those are DEF
  LABELS, not Keyed strings, so no Keyed file can touch them and a captured
  Imperial will still read "has the rank count". Renaming 11 titles into an
  Imperial ladder is a DESIGN call about what an Imperial officer is called,
  not a build call, so it is left for a named item rather than invented here.

  VOCABULARY, applied consistently: "title" -> "rank" · "royal title" ->
  "Imperial rank" · "honor" -> "Imperial favor" (that one lives on the def).
  ============================================================================
-->
<LanguageData>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       1. A CAPTURED OR DOWNED IMPERIAL WHO HOLDS A RANK
       Empire_Royal_* kinds keep spawning and keep raiding us. Select one on
       the map, or take one prisoner, and the Royalty ITab reads its rank off
       the pawn - no player title, no favour and no quest involved.
       ================================================================== -->
  <RoyalTitleTooltipHasTitle>{PAWN_labelShort} holds the Imperial rank of {TITLE}, granted by {FACTION_name}.</RoyalTitleTooltipHasTitle>
  <RoyalTitleTooltipConceited>{PAWN_labelShort} will demand that this rank's privileges be fully respected.</RoyalTitleTooltipConceited>
  <RoyalTitleTooltipNonConceited>{PAWN_labelShort} is flexible about this rank's privileges.</RoyalTitleTooltipNonConceited>
  <CurrentTitle>Current rank</CurrentTitle>

  <!-- The prisoner recruitment-difficulty breakdown, which is where a captured
       Imperial officer's rank shows up as a number the player argues with. -->
  <RecruitmentResistanceRoyalTitleOffset>{0} rank</RecruitmentResistanceRoyalTitleOffset>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       2. THE STAT CARD AND INSPECT LINE OF LOOTED IMPERIAL GEAR
       Prestige/cataphract armour, persona weapons and the Royalty implants are
       craftable or lootable and NOT faction-gated, so a colony that will never
       hold a rank still reads these every time it inspects a corpse's kit.
       ================================================================== -->
  <Stat_Thing_MinimumRoyalTitle_Name>Minimum Imperial rank ({FACTION_name})</Stat_Thing_MinimumRoyalTitle_Name>
  <Stat_Thing_MinimumRoyalTitle_Desc>{FACTION_name} has laws which limit the use of this implant to those holding specific Imperial ranks. Simply having the implant installed is undetectable, but if you use it, there is a chance they will detect the psychic emissions. This will cause diplomatic consequences.</Stat_Thing_MinimumRoyalTitle_Desc>
  <Stat_Thing_Weapon_MinimumRoyalTitle_Desc>{FACTION_name} has laws which limit the use of this weapon to those holding specific Imperial ranks. Each time you attack with the weapon, there is a chance they will detect the psychic emissions. This will cause diplomatic consequences.</Stat_Thing_Weapon_MinimumRoyalTitle_Desc>
  <Stat_Thing_MinimumRoyalTitle_Level_Desc>Each upgrade level of this implant requires a specific Imperial rank in {FACTION_name} to be used legally.</Stat_Thing_MinimumRoyalTitle_Level_Desc>
  <Stat_Thing_Apparel_MaxSatisfiedTitle>Max satisfied rank</Stat_Thing_Apparel_MaxSatisfiedTitle>
  <Stat_Thing_Apparel_MaxSatisfiedTitle_Desc>Highest Imperial rank whose apparel requirements are satisfied by this.</Stat_Thing_Apparel_MaxSatisfiedTitle_Desc>
  <Stat_Thing_Ingestible_MaxSatisfiedTitle>Max satisfied rank</Stat_Thing_Ingestible_MaxSatisfiedTitle>
  <Stat_Thing_Ingestible_MaxSatisfiedTitle_Desc>The highest Imperial rank whose food requirements are satisfied by this.</Stat_Thing_Ingestible_MaxSatisfiedTitle_Desc>
  <MinimumRoyalTitleInspectString>Minimum Imperial rank ({FACTION_name}): {TITLE}</MinimumRoyalTitleInspectString>

  <!-- The confirmation the player gets for installing or upgrading a LOOTED
       Imperial implant, which is the only way this colony will ever hold one. -->
  <RoyalImplantIllegalUseWarning>Under the laws of {FACTION_name}, only those holding the Imperial rank of {TITLE} may lawfully use a {IMPLANT}.\n\n{VIOLATIONTRIGGER}, there is a chance {FACTION_name} will detect its psychic signature. This will lead to diplomatic consequences.</RoyalImplantIllegalUseWarning>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       3. THE LAW-VIOLATION LETTER
       ⭐ The darkening makes this MORE reachable, not less: the colony gets
       caught precisely BECAUSE it holds no Imperial rank. Fires on using a
       looted psychic amplifier or persona weapon.
       ================================================================== -->
  <LetterLawViolationDetectedLabel>Imperial law: {PAWN_labelShort}</LetterLawViolationDetectedLabel>
  <LetterLawViolationDetectedForbiddenThingUse>{FACTION_name} has detected {PAWN_labelShort}'s illegal use of: {CULPRIT} (detection chance {CHANCE}).\n\nUnder the laws of {FACTION_name}, only those holding the Imperial rank of {TITLE} may use {CULPRIT}.\n\nAs a penalty, your faction relations have fallen by {GOODWILL}.</LetterLawViolationDetectedForbiddenThingUse>

</LanguageData>
